<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Economic Policy (Bolivia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1985</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Supreme Decree 21060</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The New Economic Policy was the stabilisation programme introduced in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-paz-estenssoro">Víctor Paz Estenssoro</a> through Supreme Decree 21060 of August 1985. It ended hyperinflation by floating the currency, freeing prices and cutting public spending. The closure of most state <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mines and the dismissal of more than 20,000 miners broke the power of the mining unions and drove migration to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-alto">El Alto</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chapare-province">Chapare</a>.</p></div>
